<title>UK: ICCO details result of cocoa buffer stock sale.</title>
<headline>ICCO details result of cocoa buffer stock sale.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The International Cocoa Organization (ICCO) said the 4,250 tonne buffer-stock sale earlier on Friday was completed at the following prices.</p>
<p> ORIGIN	    TONNES	QUALITY	U.S. DOLLAR</p>
<p>PRICE/TONNE</p>
<p> Ivory Coast	    6	   FF	     $1,195</p>
<p> Ivory Coast	  100	   GF	     $1,330</p>
<p> Ivory Coast	   76	   GF	     $1,330</p>
<p> Ivory Coast	  152	   FF	     $1,275</p>
<p> Ivory Coast	  101	   GF	     $1,343</p>
<p> Ivory Coast	   51	   FF	     $1,275</p>
<p> Nigeria		582	   GF	     $1,320</p>
<p> Nigeria	    2,023	   FF	     $1,255</p>
<p> Nigeria		131	   GF	     $1,330</p>
<p> Ivory Coast	  501	  FAQ	     $1,195-$1,205</p>
<p> Ivory Coast	  199	  FAQ	     $1,212</p>
<p> Ivory Coast	  126	  FAQ	     $1,195</p>
<p> Nigeria		203	  FAQ	     $1,195-$1,221</p>
<p>(GF=good fermented, FF=fair fermented, FAQ=fair to average quality)</p>
<p>The ICCO said the carry for forward delivery was calculated at $12 per tonne per month.</p>
<p>--Christopher Lyddon,  London Newsroom 044 71 542 7928.</p>
